{"name":"Light Incense","hex":"#efdcbe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"incense","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Biotic material that releases fragrant smoke when burnt, often used in religious rites or for aesthetic reasons.","The fragrant smoke released by burning incense (sense 1)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set on fire; to inflame; to kindle; to burn.","To anger; to infuriate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incense"}],"entries":[{"title":"Incense","blocks":[{"text":"Incense is an aromatic biotic material that releases fragrant smoke when burnt. The term is used for either the material or the aroma. Incense is used for aesthetic reasons, religious worship, aromatherapy, meditation, and ceremonial reasons. It may also be used as a simple deodorant or insect repellent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/R%C3%B6kelse_SSB_Helga_Trefaldighet_gif.gif/330px-R%C3%B6kelse_SSB_Helga_Trefaldighet_gif.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incense","wikidata":"Q273131"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Incenselonghua.jpg/500px-Incenselonghua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Incenselonghua.jpg/500px-Incenselonghua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Burning incense at the Longhua Temple","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIncenselonghua.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg/500px-Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg/1280px-Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg/500px-Smoke_Incense_AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smoke from incense stick","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke_Incense_AB.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Qustul_Incense_Burner%2C_Qustal%2C_Nubia%2C_Cemetery_L%2C_tomb_24%2C_A-Group%2C_3200-3000_BC%2C_limestone_-_Oriental_Institute_Museum%2C_University_of_Chicago_-_DSC08007.JPG/500px-Qustul_Incense_Burner%2C_Qustal%2C_Nubia%2C_Cemetery_L%2C_tomb_24%2C_A-Group%2C_3200-3000_BC%2C_limestone_-_Oriental_Institute_Museum%2C_University_of_Chicago_-_DSC08007.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia